From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: brennoflavio <contato@brennoflavio.com.br>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 15:39:07 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] network: discover startup timezone and location from exit IP

Probe https://api.ip.sb/geoip before ICU/V8 initialization using the
configured HTTP connection and proxy authentication. Require HTTP 200,
a bounded JSON response, a valid IP, installed IANA TZif data, and finite
coordinates. Apply discovered timezone to Date/Intl and seed permission-gated
geolocation with conservative 50 km accuracy.

Bound the transfer to five seconds and fall back with a warning to
America/Los_Angeles and approximate San Francisco coordinates. Explicit
--timezone remains authoritative; locale is unchanged. Skip public discovery
in the upstream unit-test binary.

Make direct mode ignore inherited curl proxies and prevent NO_PROXY from
bypassing an explicit proxy. Keep bearer authentication in proxy-only headers
for both discovery and page traffic. Discovery is process-startup-only;
rotating exits and CDP proxy changes still require restart.

Validation: debug and release builds; 1658 existing upstream tests; 13 temporary
CDP/proxy scenarios including timeout, invalid data, CA ownership, bearer
isolation, permissions, and explicit overrides. Live direct and residential-
proxy requests agree with browser timezone/coordinates. Benchmark timezone-
present and timezone-matches-ip pass in both modes (127/130 overall; unrelated
stack-depth timing, WebGL/SVG, offline audio failures). No new unit tests.
